    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Bundles with 5+ options where no SBQQ__OptionGroup__c is used to group them.
Why it matters: Sales reps face a flat list of 5+ checkboxes with no visual grouping — configuration errors spike, deal velocity slows, and complex bundles get under-configured because reps miss options.
Suppress a finding: when the bundle is intentionally simple and option groups would add unnecessary clicks for a small option set.
Disable the detector: only if your bundles are uniformly small (&lt;5 options). Most orgs with complex bundles should leave this on.</value></values>
